WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:02.270
Speaker 1: Let's talk about that.

00:00:02.270 --> 00:00:07.120
I'm really glad that something I've been saying
for a couple of months now is getting more

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.120
attention.

00:00:08.120 --> 00:00:11.000
It's not getting more attention from me saying
it ought to be clear.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.230
What I mean is I'm glad other people are coming
to the same conclusion, which is that by all

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:20.650
accounts, Republicans should do very well
in the upcoming midterms.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:25.289
Now we're under six under nine months away
from the midterms.

00:00:25.289 --> 00:00:32.080
One of the best chances at Republicans not
doing well is the explosion of the internal

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:36.940
disagreements and civil war that we're increasingly
seeing within the Republican Party, which

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:38.390
we have been covering.

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:45.070
David Siders and Natalie Allison wrote about
this in a piece for Politico called Trump's

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:50.670
circular firing squad threatens Republican
midterm gains.

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:55.080
And this outlines a lot of what we've been
saying.

00:00:55.080 --> 00:01:00.440
And the article says nine months before the
midterms, nearly everything is falling the

00:01:00.440 --> 00:01:05.140
Republican Party's way from Joe Biden's dismal
approval ratings to rising gas prices and

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:07.509
a seemingly never ending pandemic.

00:01:07.509 --> 00:01:13.439
Yet as the RNC concluded its winter meeting
here on Friday, it was censuring two of its

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:19.999
own representatives, Liz Cheney and Adam Kinzinger,
and decrying the House's Jan. six select committee

00:01:19.999 --> 00:01:24.740
for what Ronna McDaniel, the RNC chair, called
the quote persecution of ordinary citizens

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:28.900
who engaged in legitimate political discourse
that had nothing to do with violence at the

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:29.900
Capitol.

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:35.259
In a year in which even many Democrats acknowledge
the Republicans will likely win the House.

00:01:35.259 --> 00:01:39.819
And despite Republican lawmakers and strategists
pleading with Republicans to keep their focus

00:01:39.819 --> 00:01:46.799
on pocket book issues and on Biden, the RNC
is still recasting the events of January 6th

00:01:46.799 --> 00:01:51.960
and chasing down enemies of the defeated former
President Donald Trump.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:58.549
They go on to say for all the energy he creates
at the party's grassroots, his stranglehold

00:01:58.549 --> 00:02:04.829
on the party is emerging as one of the biggest
threats to the Republicans otherwise bright

00:02:04.829 --> 00:02:06.819
prospects in November.

00:02:06.819 --> 00:02:10.060
He has singled out 10 House Republicans for
extinction.

00:02:10.060 --> 00:02:15.160
He's attacking Republican governors backing
primary challengers meddling in Senate races,

00:02:15.160 --> 00:02:20.590
where it may lead to the nomination of flawed
candidates ill suited for a general election.

00:02:20.590 --> 00:02:24.990
He's fomenting rebellion against the party's
Senate leader, Mitch McConnell, and this week

00:02:24.990 --> 00:02:26.340
in Salt Lake City.

00:02:26.340 --> 00:02:31.220
It was David Bossie, the former Trump deputy
campaign manager, leading the effort to kick

00:02:31.220 --> 00:02:33.960
Cheney and Kinzinger to the curb.

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:39.280
Read the entire article, but it gets to the
really key point, which is a sad point for

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:40.280
us, right?

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:41.440
I care about the left.

00:02:41.440 --> 00:02:44.350
The left is really failing right now.

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:49.520
It's just really failing in terms of setting
itself up to do well.

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:50.520
Nine.

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:56.371
Months from now in the midterms, sadly, like
it, it it really pains me to admit this, but

00:02:56.371 --> 00:03:03.600
the person best positioned to save the country
from Trumpian insanity is Trump and Trumpists

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:06.790
sabotaging their own midterms.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:10.730
It's tragically sad that this is the case
for the Democratic Party right now.

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:15.700
But with under nine months to go until the
midterms, I'll take any help I can get.

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:21.470
And so when we see Trump doing this insane
stuff, we see Republicans censuring Adam Kinzinger

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:22.500
and Liz Cheney.

00:03:22.500 --> 00:03:27.310
Last week, I told you that George W. Bush,
from another wing of the Republican Party,

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:34.550
has donated the maximum allowed by law to
both Lisa Murkowski and Liz Cheney, to people,

00:03:34.550 --> 00:03:37.880
to Republicans that supported the impeachment
of Donald Trump.

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:41.040
I will take all of it because they're all
terrible.

00:03:41.040 --> 00:03:43.060
Remember, Liz Cheney is not our friend.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:47.280
Liz Cheney, when the rubber met the road,
voted with Trump most of the time.

00:03:47.280 --> 00:03:49.320
So it's all bad.

00:03:49.320 --> 00:03:50.320
We're maybe.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:55.650
I mean, listen, are we even better off with
a non Trump Republican than a Trump Republican?

00:03:55.650 --> 00:04:00.020
If the non Trump Republican is slightly less
crazy but more likely to get their policies

00:04:00.020 --> 00:04:01.020
passed?

00:04:01.020 --> 00:04:02.640
We're poorly off no matter what.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:07.730
So I would love to see the Democratic Party
get it together and take advantage of this

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:13.670
situation where, you know, historically looking,
it should not be a great midterm for Democrats,

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:15.400
but maybe it could be.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:18.159
This is the biggest gift we could imagine.

00:04:18.159 --> 00:04:22.509
And so we have to do everything we can to
encourage the Civil War to continue.

00:04:22.509 --> 00:04:27.480
We'll have more on this on our Instagram page,
which you can find at David Pakman show.

